#!/usr/bin/env python3
# sunshine-vd — on-demand virtual display for Sunshine on GNOME (Wayland).
#
# How it works
#   * The kernel force-enables a free connector on the GPU and loads a custom
#     EDID on it (drm.edid_firmware=<conn>:edid/sunshine-vd.bin video=<conn>:e).
#     GNOME sees it as one more monitor offering your clients' resolutions.
#   * Sunshine runs "sunshine-vd start" (global_prep_cmd "do") when a stream
#     starts: the current display layout is saved, the virtual display becomes
#     the only active output in the mode closest to what the client asked for,
#     and GNOME is kept from blanking the screen.
#   * Sunshine runs "sunshine-vd stop" (global_prep_cmd "undo") when the app is
#     closed: the saved layout is restored.
#
# Subcommands: start | stop | idle | save-layout | status | modes | connectors |
#              doctor | make-edid | sunshine-conf | conf-path | conf-get
#
# "start" and "stop" ALWAYS exit 0: if something goes wrong, Sunshine still
# streams (whatever display is active) instead of refusing to launch.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

